# How this project's own code in shim/src/dll/ is written (D3D12Api.cpp, XellHook.*, XefgAnswers.cpp, XefgHook.cpp,
# HookUtil.cpp, XellDriver.cpp, GpuInfo.*, DxbcChecksum.h, LdrNotify.h), for clang-format (checked with clang-format
# 19; the "Kind" of AlignTrailingComments needs clang-format 16 or newer). IgdextApiDll*.cpp in this folder come from
# dxvk-igdext and are written as shim/.clang-format says: for them, name that file
# (clang-format --style=file:<path to shim/.clang-format>).
#
# For new and changed lines only. Do not run clang-format over a whole file here: about 12 % of the lines of those
# files would change (2026-11). clang-format cannot keep two statements on one line, which this code has in many
# places, and the files do not agree on a space after a cast (XellHook.cpp and the three files that were part of it
# have it, the others do not).
#
# 4 spaces. Every brace on its own line; a short if, loop or block may stay on one line. "Type* name". No limit to
# the length of a line: the lines stay as they were broken. { 1, 2 } with spaces inside. Trailing comments stay where
# they were put. Comments are wrapped by hand, and the includes stay in the order they are in.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 0
PointerAlignment: Left
BreakBeforeBraces: Allman
AccessModifierOffset: -4
IndentExternBlock: NoIndent
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: AllIfsAndElse
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Always
AlwaysBreakTemplateDeclarations: No
Cpp11BracedListStyle: false
SpaceAfterCStyleCast: true
AlignTrailingComments:
  Kind: Leave
MaxEmptyLinesToKeep: 2
ReflowComments: false
SortIncludes: false
